  {
   "type": "text",
   "id": "takeaway",
   "x": 60.0,
   "y": 1147.0,
   "width": 980,
   "height": 60,
   "text": "The C++ engine is a passive library with exactly two Rust callers: the IIIF dispatcher\n(one coarse serve call per request) and the Lua binding layer (fine-grained image-handle\ncalls, driven by the script). Control flow never starts in C++.",
   "originalText": "The C++ engine is a passive library with exactly two Rust callers: the IIIF dispatcher\n(one coarse serve call per request) and the Lua binding layer (fine-grained image-handle\ncalls, driven by the script). Control flow never starts in C++.",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
